# A patch must round-trip byte-exact: the files it applies to are LF, so letting
# the working copy get CRLF line endings makes `git apply` reject it.
*.patch -text

# The generated shader sources are hashed into bytecode.manifest, so their bytes
# must be the same on every host: `core.autocrlf` would otherwise hand a Windows
# clone CRLF and the Mac LF, giving one committed source two digests and putting
# the two hosts in a permanent rebuild loop (D5). The compiled blobs are binary and
# must never be touched at all.
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/*.hlsl text eol=lf
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/*.metal text eol=lf
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/*.rs text eol=lf
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/bytecode.manifest text eol=lf
# The digest of the review.glsl the set was generated from — build.rs compares it
# against the file's own hash, so a CRLF conversion here would make every build warn.
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/review.glsl.sha256 text eol=lf
# And review.glsl itself, since that hash is taken over its bytes.
crates/render/src/shaders/review.glsl text eol=lf
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/*.dxbc binary
crates/render/src/shaders/generated/*.metallib binary
